{
  "header": {
    "name": "RAID",
    "size": [128, 12],
    "code": "RAID",
    "type": "SINGLE",
    "publicCode": true,
    "legacyVersion": 6
  },
  "texts": {
    "briefing": "You've been briefed. You need to destroy\ncritical military targets and land on\nthe aircraft carrier. Now you are on the\nrunway loaded with everything you need.\nA wingman and an LRM-1 (Little Runt\nModel 1, the newest minaturized tank)\nhave been assigned to protect you. But\nthen...\n\nYou notice enemy aircraft on the radar.\nA missile hits a fuel tank. Your run-\nway starts exploding. You have to jet-\ntison your heavy equipment so you can\ntake off quickly. A nuke vaporizes\nyour base. \n\nYou know that you can't destroy the\ncritical targets with just 5 missiles.\nBut you know that an LRM-1 is station-\ned next to the aircraft carrier. You\nhave to get there.",
    "success": "On the way to the aircraft carrier,\nyour radar spots a turret. You ready\na missile and fire it just as the\nturret comes into view. It never has\na chance to shoot.\n\nYou land on the aircraft carrier, get\nout, and start running toward the LRM-1.\n\nYou talk to the computer (it is much too\nsmall for a human to be in it) and tell\nit your problem.\n\nThe LR speeds away and you walk back to\nyour jet. You hear machine-gun fire and\nbuildings exploding. A jet flies over-\nhead and your wingman toasts it with\nmissiles.\n\nYou check on the LR and find that it is\ntoasting buildings at an incredibly high\nrate. When the last building vanishes in\nsmoke and flame, you radio it to come\nback to the aircraft carrier.\n\nFive minutes later, the small drone speeds\nacross the water, and stops next to your\nplane."
  },
